1
00:00:03,683 --> 00:00:06,723
- Big smiles, please. - Cheese.

2
00:00:08,663 --> 00:00:10,163
You look so beautiful.

3
00:00:10,263 --> 00:00:12,063
Oh, you're the best.

4
00:00:18,603 --> 00:00:19,633
What?

5
00:00:22,443 --> 00:00:23,903
We should wrap things up now.

6
00:00:23,973 --> 00:00:26,443
I'll pack up, so you can head out first.

7
00:00:26,573 --> 00:00:28,443
Okay, break time, okay.

8
00:00:28,583 --> 00:00:30,683
Honey, it's so cold.

9
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,803
Hey, let go of me!

10
00:00:58,143 --> 00:00:59,213
Stay still!

11
00:01:00,943 --> 00:01:02,643
- Calm down! - Do you want to die?

12
00:01:20,063 --> 00:01:21,493
- Get out, you punk. - I'm not getting out, you bastards.

13
00:01:21,563 --> 00:01:22,703
Hey, you guys.

14
00:01:24,263 --> 00:01:25,873
Who are you? Let go of me.

15
00:01:25,933 --> 00:01:28,603
Who are you guys? You've got the wrong person.

16
00:01:30,043 --> 00:01:31,043
Where is this?

17
00:01:31,343 --> 00:01:33,173
- Where am I? Who are you people? - Ji Won Ho.

18
00:01:35,743 --> 00:01:36,813
You...

19
00:01:36,813 --> 00:01:38,313
What do you think you're doing?

20
00:01:41,183 --> 00:01:42,183
Hee Ju...

21
00:01:43,453 --> 00:01:44,453
Hee Ju...

22
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:53,633
Just trust me.

23
00:01:54,193 --> 00:01:57,233
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

24
00:02:01,773 --> 00:02:02,973
Hee Ju.

25
00:02:02,973 --> 00:02:04,173
Hee Ju!

26
00:02:13,013 --> 00:02:14,153
Let's go fulfill...

27
00:02:15,183 --> 00:02:16,223
that promise.

28
00:02:16,583 --> 00:02:17,623
Wait a minute!

29
00:02:19,053 --> 00:02:20,193
I'm getting a divorce soon,

30
00:02:20,553 --> 00:02:21,993
and once things are over between Mi Young and me,

31
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:24,323
you'll have your chance with her, Calvin.

32
00:02:24,323 --> 00:02:26,093
Aren't you jumping the gun?

33
00:02:29,463 --> 00:02:30,963
- Let's go. - Hey!

34
00:02:31,363 --> 00:02:32,733
Let go of me, you bastards!

35
00:02:33,373 --> 00:02:34,373
Hey.

36
00:02:37,203 --> 00:02:38,203
Hee Ju.

37
00:02:39,413 --> 00:02:40,413
Hee Ju.

38
00:02:40,943 --> 00:02:44,043
Are you okay? Hee Ju. Oh no...

39
00:02:46,053 --> 00:02:47,653
Just hang in there.

40
00:02:53,553 --> 00:02:56,323
Do you think you'll get away with this, you bastards?

41
00:03:03,263 --> 00:03:04,303
And where is this place?

42
00:03:05,063 --> 00:03:07,503
What kind of stunt are you pulling on me now?

43
00:03:10,203 --> 00:03:11,443
This is my vacation home.

44
00:03:13,143 --> 00:03:14,143
Vacation home?

45
00:03:14,613 --> 00:03:15,783
The view isn't bad, is it?

46
00:03:16,543 --> 00:03:19,983
This is where my grandparents lived until they passed away.

47
00:03:20,753 --> 00:03:23,483
I come here to rest sometimes when I need to recharge.

48
00:03:25,083 --> 00:03:28,253
Then you should have come alone. I don't need to recharge.

49
00:03:35,403 --> 00:03:36,463
I wanted to,

50
00:03:37,763 --> 00:03:38,833
at least once,

51
00:03:39,903 --> 00:03:43,243
open up and tell you my deepest thoughts.

52
00:03:43,943 --> 00:03:45,543
Then you should have just said so from the beginning.

53
00:03:45,543 --> 00:03:47,943
Did you really have to put on such a violent show for this?

54
00:03:48,313 --> 00:03:51,413
We'll see if it ends as just a show after we talk.

55
00:03:53,683 --> 00:03:56,623
Don't be too nervous. I'm not trying to scare you.

56
00:03:57,023 --> 00:03:58,893
You say that after scaring me half to death.

57
00:04:00,153 --> 00:04:02,523
So what is this deep talk you wanted to have?

58
00:04:04,463 --> 00:04:07,863
If that incident hadn't happened seven years ago,

59
00:04:08,963 --> 00:04:13,473
I never would have let Mi Young go.

60
00:04:18,073 --> 00:04:19,073
Hee Ju.

61
00:04:20,073 --> 00:04:24,083
Luckily, the doctor said it's not a major fracture or injury.

62
00:04:24,683 --> 00:04:26,753
You'll be fine after a few days of rest,

63
00:04:26,813 --> 00:04:28,053
so don't worry too much.

64
00:04:28,683 --> 00:04:30,923
Still, it's a huge relief it wasn't worse.

65
00:04:31,453 --> 00:04:32,693
They tried to kill me.

66
00:04:34,623 --> 00:04:36,323
Someone pushed me...

67
00:04:38,663 --> 00:04:39,793
off the cliff.

68
00:04:40,793 --> 00:04:42,603
Hee Ju, what are you saying?

69
00:04:43,103 --> 00:04:44,563
Who would push you?

70
00:04:44,663 --> 00:04:47,033
It's true. I'm telling you, it's true!

71
00:04:47,673 --> 00:04:49,903
Someone definitely pushed me.

72
00:04:58,683 --> 00:04:59,683
I'm sure of it.

73
00:05:01,153 --> 00:05:02,783
It's still so clear.

74
00:05:03,953 --> 00:05:07,753
The feeling of someone's hands pushing my back.

75
00:05:13,293 --> 00:05:15,233
But still, that doesn't make any sense.

76
00:05:15,293 --> 00:05:17,733
Who would do such a terrible thing to you?

77
00:05:19,473 --> 00:05:20,903
I have my suspicions...

78
00:05:22,843 --> 00:05:24,073
as to who I think it was.

79
00:05:27,373 --> 00:05:28,443
Calvin.

80
00:05:30,143 --> 00:05:31,343
It was Calvin.

81
00:05:32,183 --> 00:05:33,483
He's the one who tried to kill me.

82
00:05:33,883 --> 00:05:34,883
What?

83
00:05:35,313 --> 00:05:37,883
What basis do you have for saying that?

84
00:05:37,953 --> 00:05:41,653
Calvin is the type of person who, when I said I was dating CEO Ji,

85
00:05:42,323 --> 00:05:44,723
fired me on the spot without a second thought.

86
00:05:46,233 --> 00:05:48,463
He can do anything he sets his mind to.

87
00:05:49,203 --> 00:05:51,833
He has the power and influence to do whatever he wants.

88
00:05:54,033 --> 00:05:55,403
Who else could it be but Calvin?

89
00:05:58,673 --> 00:06:00,643
Think about it, CEO Baek.

90
00:06:02,213 --> 00:06:03,213
Calvin...

91
00:06:04,213 --> 00:06:06,453
is much scarier than you think.

92
00:06:14,723 --> 00:06:15,823
Is that true?

93
00:06:17,763 --> 00:06:19,333
So your son, no...

94
00:06:20,033 --> 00:06:23,263
The child you believed was your son turned out not to be yours?

95
00:06:25,403 --> 00:06:26,703
How is that possible?

96
00:06:27,473 --> 00:06:28,673
When did you find that out?

97
00:06:29,403 --> 00:06:30,443
Three years ago.

98
00:06:31,243 --> 00:06:32,613
Three years ago?

99
00:06:33,573 --> 00:06:35,343
But I heard you only got divorced recently.

100
00:06:35,743 --> 00:06:38,613
I fought a lawsuit for three years to get custody of the child.

101
00:06:40,353 --> 00:06:41,783
But I ended up losing the case.

102
00:06:44,423 --> 00:06:45,553
Three years ago,

103
00:06:46,693 --> 00:06:50,093
the day the detailed test results came back negative for paternity,

104
00:06:51,163 --> 00:06:53,433
I happened to see Mi Young at the hospital.

105
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:57,133
She looked pregnant.

106
00:06:58,503 --> 00:07:00,173
I couldn't bring myself to say hello,

107
00:07:01,133 --> 00:07:02,903
and just watched her from a distance.

108
00:07:04,543 --> 00:07:05,573
Honestly,

109
00:07:07,143 --> 00:07:08,473
it was a truly bitter feeling.

110
00:07:13,353 --> 00:07:14,353
I, too,

111
00:07:17,353 --> 00:07:19,793
couldn't protect my child in the end.

112
00:07:21,193 --> 00:07:22,663
I haven't given up yet.

113
00:07:24,423 --> 00:07:26,033
The child I raised as my own,

114
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:30,003
I will get him back, no matter how long it takes.

115
00:07:32,703 --> 00:07:35,033
Calvin, are you telling me this because?

116
00:07:35,203 --> 00:07:37,173
I have absolutely no ulterior motives...

117
00:07:37,243 --> 00:07:38,543
or feelings for Mi Young.

118
00:07:41,273 --> 00:07:44,883
So if you're seeing Hee Ju out of resentment toward me,

119
00:07:46,753 --> 00:07:48,313
I'm asking you to stop right there.

120
00:07:57,193 --> 00:07:59,393
It's okay. I don't have an appetite.

121
00:07:59,693 --> 00:08:02,333
Still, have a bite. You need to eat to take your pills.

122
00:08:03,333 --> 00:08:04,533
What about CEO Ji?

123
00:08:05,903 --> 00:08:07,673
Why isn't CEO Ji here yet?

124
00:08:08,673 --> 00:08:11,173
I sent him a text. He'll come once he sees it.

125
00:08:12,573 --> 00:08:14,113
Are you sure you sent him a message?

126
00:08:14,943 --> 00:08:19,483
You didn't just say that without telling him, did you?

127
00:08:20,683 --> 00:08:23,923
If you really don't believe me, text him yourself.

128
00:08:30,193 --> 00:08:31,263
CEO Ji!

129
00:08:41,273 --> 00:08:43,703
Where have you been?

130
00:08:43,873 --> 00:08:45,743
I was waiting forever.

131
00:08:47,943 --> 00:08:50,513
Are you okay? Are you badly hurt?

132
00:08:51,443 --> 00:08:53,913
I thought I was going to die.

133
00:08:59,953 --> 00:09:02,823
Look, I got a big scrape here.

134
00:09:03,063 --> 00:09:06,233
I'm just glad it's not worse. Hurry and eat something.

135
00:09:06,363 --> 00:09:08,693
I don't have an appetite, and my wrist hurts...

136
00:09:08,763 --> 00:09:11,303
- You have to eat to get better. - My hand hurts. Can't you feed me?

137
00:09:11,363 --> 00:09:14,233
Oh, come on. Just eat. Here, I'll pour you some water.

138
00:09:19,243 --> 00:09:20,873
You found Hee Ju, right?

139
00:09:22,643 --> 00:09:23,683
You went through a lot.

140
00:09:25,813 --> 00:09:28,883
Where were you all day? I couldn't reach you.

141
00:09:30,023 --> 00:09:32,593
Is it that hard to send one message...

142
00:09:32,993 --> 00:09:35,023
if you can't come, or if you're going to be late?

143
00:09:35,023 --> 00:09:36,593
It's not like you were kidnapped.

144
00:09:37,723 --> 00:09:38,823
How did you know?

145
00:09:39,693 --> 00:09:43,033
- What? - I just came from seeing Calvin.

146
00:09:45,063 --> 00:09:46,173
I heard everything.

147
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:48,303
I know why Calvin got a divorce.

148
00:09:48,733 --> 00:09:49,773
Calvin...

149
00:09:51,673 --> 00:09:54,613
told you that himself?

150
00:09:55,243 --> 00:09:57,043
I guess all this time...

151
00:09:58,783 --> 00:10:00,413
I've really misjudged him.

152
00:10:01,753 --> 00:10:04,183
And I did a lot of thinking on the way over,

153
00:10:05,323 --> 00:10:08,653
and I think I've been rash about a lot of things.

154
00:10:09,693 --> 00:10:12,363
I'll take care of Hee Ju until she gets discharged.

155
00:10:14,993 --> 00:10:17,763
And that written pledge...

156
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:22,803
Let's just forget about it.

157
00:10:23,573 --> 00:10:25,773
I'll take care of everything.

158
00:10:26,473 --> 00:10:27,913
So Hee Ju was right.

159
00:10:29,683 --> 00:10:30,983
Hee Ju said...

160
00:10:32,113 --> 00:10:33,853
that Calvin was a dangerous man.

161
00:10:35,153 --> 00:10:36,883
I mean, how could you change your mind...

162
00:10:37,353 --> 00:10:38,953
just because of what Calvin said?

163
00:10:39,253 --> 00:10:42,323
No, it's not like I changed my mind just because of that.

164
00:10:44,323 --> 00:10:48,363
Anyway, I'm leaving. Take good care of Hee Ju.

165
00:10:50,003 --> 00:10:51,403
He's a lot like you.

166
00:10:55,403 --> 00:10:56,443
Calvin.

167
00:10:57,743 --> 00:10:59,913
He said he was desperate to get his child back.

168
00:11:02,613 --> 00:11:05,753
And it suddenly made me think of you.

169
00:11:07,413 --> 00:11:08,753
I hate to admit it,

170
00:11:09,683 --> 00:11:10,723
but you two...

171
00:11:13,693 --> 00:11:14,793
are a lot alike.

172
00:11:15,023 --> 00:11:16,693
What's your point?

173
00:11:17,463 --> 00:11:19,993
Honestly, I never really understood...

174
00:11:20,063 --> 00:11:22,093
why you used to like a guy like that.

175
00:11:23,903 --> 00:11:24,963
But...

176
00:11:26,773 --> 00:11:28,133
now I think...

177
00:11:30,573 --> 00:11:31,943
I kind of get it.

178
00:11:38,983 --> 00:11:40,853
I'm sorry it took me so long...

179
00:11:43,353 --> 00:11:44,783
to understand, Mi Young.

180
00:12:03,103 --> 00:12:04,143
Did you hear?

181
00:12:04,843 --> 00:12:08,273
CEO Ji is busy taking care of his young girlfriend,

182
00:12:08,443 --> 00:12:10,413
so he's stuck to her like glue.

183
00:12:11,283 --> 00:12:13,713
Well, that's over as of today.

184
00:12:14,413 --> 00:12:16,723
- What? - She's being discharged today.

185
00:12:17,183 --> 00:12:20,053
So, are they coming here together later?

186
00:12:20,193 --> 00:12:22,193
Why would they come here together?

187
00:12:22,293 --> 00:12:25,493
His girlfriend's a writer for our company, you know.

188
00:12:25,563 --> 00:12:26,593
She's an official employee.

189
00:12:26,693 --> 00:12:28,133
You call that being an official employee?

190
00:12:28,193 --> 00:12:29,333
It was pure nepotism.

191
00:12:29,663 --> 00:12:30,833
And I'm dead set against...

192
00:12:31,203 --> 00:12:33,473
that woman coming back to this company.

193
00:12:34,833 --> 00:12:36,843
All because of one woman, the CEO of a company...

194
00:12:37,643 --> 00:12:39,643
How many days has he been away from the office?

195
00:12:46,453 --> 00:12:49,523
He doesn't pull any punches.

196
00:12:50,153 --> 00:12:53,323
He really keeps business and personal matters separate.

197
00:12:53,923 --> 00:12:55,353
Now that his affair is out in the open,

198
00:12:55,693 --> 00:12:57,263
it's game over for him.

199
00:12:59,663 --> 00:13:01,363
We don't even need the Domestic Affairs Investigation.

200
00:13:01,793 --> 00:13:03,703
We should ride this momentum and just...

201
00:13:04,663 --> 00:13:06,103
go straight to trial.

202
00:13:11,903 --> 00:13:14,743
Affairs are my specialty,

203
00:13:15,443 --> 00:13:18,643
and no one I've ever caught for it has ever gotten away with it.

204
00:13:19,783 --> 00:13:23,223
He said he was going to end things with her.

205
00:13:24,023 --> 00:13:26,393
Who did? Your husband?

206
00:13:26,753 --> 00:13:28,223
I'm not sure,

207
00:13:30,463 --> 00:13:32,093
but I don't think he was serious...

208
00:13:32,093 --> 00:13:33,433
about being in a relationship with her.

209
00:13:33,763 --> 00:13:35,293
Let me tell you,

210
00:13:35,733 --> 00:13:38,963
nobody ever plans to have an affair.

211
00:13:39,533 --> 00:13:40,703
Looking back,

212
00:13:41,503 --> 00:13:43,203
I think it was because of what happened.

213
00:13:44,643 --> 00:13:45,643
That day...

214
00:13:47,113 --> 00:13:50,083
when I found out about his pain.

215
00:13:52,583 --> 00:13:55,453
The very fact that I knew about it...

216
00:13:56,153 --> 00:13:57,583
must have made him really uncomfortable.

217
00:13:59,723 --> 00:14:01,993
He was so uncomfortable and bothered by it...

218
00:14:03,493 --> 00:14:05,463
that he acted out in rebellion.

219
00:14:05,963 --> 00:14:08,633
Deciding to start dating in the middle of a lawsuit...

220
00:14:08,693 --> 00:14:10,363
was your husband's choice.

221
00:14:10,603 --> 00:14:12,363
It's not like you pushed him into it, Mi Young.

222
00:14:13,503 --> 00:14:16,543
Don't get too hung up on these petty feelings.

223
00:14:17,503 --> 00:14:19,003
Let's remember why we started this.

224
00:14:20,813 --> 00:14:23,183
Why you, Mi Young,

225
00:14:23,943 --> 00:14:25,613
decided to get a divorce in the first place.

226
00:14:30,183 --> 00:14:33,823
(Maesan Hospital)

227
00:14:39,663 --> 00:14:40,663
What?

228
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:42,393
I'm being discharged today.

229
00:14:42,963 --> 00:14:45,233
What? A discharge party?

230
00:14:46,903 --> 00:14:47,903
I can't.

231
00:14:48,673 --> 00:14:51,843
My boyfriend said he was picking me up today.

232
00:14:53,843 --> 00:14:55,213
I'll introduce you later.

233
00:14:57,713 --> 00:14:59,553
Hey, I'll call you later. Bye.

234
00:15:17,303 --> 00:15:19,873
I'll call you a taxi, so tell me your address.

235
00:15:20,173 --> 00:15:23,943
Did CEO Ji really send you in his place?

236
00:15:24,273 --> 00:15:26,773
Why else would I have come all this way?

237
00:15:29,313 --> 00:15:30,313
That's so cruel.

238
00:15:30,583 --> 00:15:32,753
How could he not even show up on the day I'm discharged?

239
00:15:32,983 --> 00:15:35,853
He won't be showing up from now on, either.

240
00:15:36,483 --> 00:15:37,483
What did you say?

241
00:15:37,653 --> 00:15:38,653
Won Ho...

242
00:15:39,593 --> 00:15:41,053
isn't going to see you anymore, Hee Ju.

243
00:15:42,453 --> 00:15:43,463
What?

244
00:15:43,793 --> 00:15:45,693
How could you be so heartless?

245
00:15:46,363 --> 00:15:48,563
Breaking up with her like that.

246
00:15:50,103 --> 00:15:53,433
- That young woman must be furious. - I had no choice.

247
00:15:53,703 --> 00:15:55,333
This is the only way to end things.

248
00:15:55,503 --> 00:15:56,973
I don't know...

249
00:15:57,543 --> 00:15:59,713
I don't think it'll be that easy.

250
00:16:00,213 --> 00:16:02,843
That desperation to be by your side,

251
00:16:02,843 --> 00:16:04,883
even if she had to pretend to be your girlfriend...

252
00:16:04,883 --> 00:16:07,053
Do you think feelings like that just vanish overnight?

253
00:16:07,513 --> 00:16:09,113
How do you know so much?

254
00:16:09,183 --> 00:16:11,183
Coming from the man who learned about love from books.

255
00:16:11,183 --> 00:16:12,583
What's that supposed to mean?

256
00:16:12,753 --> 00:16:15,453
I'll have you know I graduated from Hankuk University.

257
00:16:15,923 --> 00:16:16,923
Gosh.

258
00:16:17,623 --> 00:16:20,133
Anyway, it's completely over now.

259
00:16:20,893 --> 00:16:22,133
If you say so,

260
00:16:22,963 --> 00:16:24,703
we'll just have to wait and see.

261
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,603
Every single day, it's these paper cups.

262
00:16:34,743 --> 00:16:35,743
Anyway,

263
00:16:36,543 --> 00:16:38,883
the biggest hurdle left for you...

264
00:16:39,783 --> 00:16:41,053
is the Domestic Affairs Investigation.

265
00:16:41,653 --> 00:16:42,753
The Domestic Affairs Investigation?

266
00:16:43,153 --> 00:16:46,023
These investigators are all sharp, just like me.

267
00:16:46,553 --> 00:16:48,953
Provoking hotheads like you...

268
00:16:49,023 --> 00:16:51,963
until you show your true colours is a piece of cake for them.

269
00:16:52,063 --> 00:16:54,233
What's wrong with my temper?

270
00:16:54,293 --> 00:16:55,763
See? You can't even hold it in for a second.

271
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:56,833
Good grief.

272
00:16:57,633 --> 00:16:58,963
Domestic Affairs Investigation or whatever,

273
00:16:59,033 --> 00:17:01,403
I'm done fighting with Mi Young.

274
00:17:01,773 --> 00:17:03,273
I'm just going to let things run their course.

275
00:17:03,543 --> 00:17:04,673
Dragging out this lawsuit...

276
00:17:04,743 --> 00:17:05,973
will just drain us both.

277
00:17:06,213 --> 00:17:07,213
So...

278
00:17:07,343 --> 00:17:09,683
are you going to give them everything they want and end it?

279
00:17:09,843 --> 00:17:13,553
Of course not. I have a line I won't cross.

280
00:17:14,813 --> 00:17:17,023
They won't cross that line, will they?

281
00:17:17,423 --> 00:17:18,423
Listen.

282
00:17:18,953 --> 00:17:20,723
You know who the opposing counsel is, don't you?

283
00:17:20,723 --> 00:17:21,753
I do.

284
00:17:21,893 --> 00:17:23,723
Jeon Chi Hyun. Once she bites, she never lets go.

285
00:17:23,863 --> 00:17:26,363
So don't you let your guard down until the very end.

286
00:17:26,463 --> 00:17:28,933
Let your guard down for a second, and she'll cross the line...

287
00:17:28,993 --> 00:17:30,663
and take you for everything you've got.

288
00:17:36,143 --> 00:17:37,143
Okay.

289
00:17:40,243 --> 00:17:42,243
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

290
00:17:47,313 --> 00:17:48,313
Calvin.

291
00:17:49,253 --> 00:17:50,623
It was Calvin.

292
00:17:51,553 --> 00:17:52,953
He's the one who tried to kill me.

293
00:17:56,793 --> 00:17:57,793
No.

294
00:17:58,963 --> 00:18:00,693
There's no way Calvin would do that.

295
00:18:02,363 --> 00:18:03,403
Manipulate?

296
00:18:03,933 --> 00:18:05,703
I am actually holding myself back.

297
00:18:06,803 --> 00:18:10,803
All I want is for Mi Young to be happy.

298
00:18:12,373 --> 00:18:13,543
You know, Mi Young...

299
00:18:14,773 --> 00:18:15,873
If by any chance...

300
00:18:16,513 --> 00:18:18,143
If you're ever having a hard time...

301
00:18:19,383 --> 00:18:21,413
He can do anything he sets his mind to.

302
00:18:22,453 --> 00:18:25,023
He has the power and influence to do whatever he wants.

303
00:18:26,193 --> 00:18:27,623
Who else could it be but Calvin?

304
00:18:32,123 --> 00:18:35,493
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

305
00:18:35,563 --> 00:18:38,233
(Calvin)

306
00:18:43,903 --> 00:18:46,543
It's me. By any chance,

307
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:48,613
are you free this evening?

308
00:19:06,493 --> 00:19:09,163
But why is it so empty?

309
00:19:10,633 --> 00:19:11,633
It is, isn't it?

310
00:19:11,933 --> 00:19:13,273
Why are there no customers today?

311
00:19:14,003 --> 00:19:15,003
Don't tell me...

312
00:19:15,273 --> 00:19:17,303
you turned away customers because of me, did you?

313
00:19:17,743 --> 00:19:18,773
Of course not.

314
00:19:19,073 --> 00:19:21,113
I may not look like it, but I'm a businessman.

315
00:19:24,743 --> 00:19:25,743
Let's eat.

316
00:19:32,823 --> 00:19:34,753
I'm sorry, but we're fully booked tonight.

317
00:19:36,863 --> 00:19:39,163
The chef said he prepared something special,

318
00:19:39,563 --> 00:19:40,993
so I hope you like it.

319
00:19:47,773 --> 00:19:48,773
It's delicious.

320
00:19:49,673 --> 00:19:50,843
It's really delicious.

321
00:19:51,103 --> 00:19:52,103
I'm glad.

322
00:19:52,913 --> 00:19:53,913
Oh, right.

323
00:19:54,073 --> 00:19:56,113
You said you had something to tell me when you called.

324
00:19:56,483 --> 00:19:57,643
May I ask what it was?

325
00:20:00,883 --> 00:20:01,883
Well...

326
00:20:03,783 --> 00:20:06,493
A little while ago, Hee Ju went on an outdoor shoot...

327
00:20:06,553 --> 00:20:07,953
and had an accident.

328
00:20:08,653 --> 00:20:10,323
She slipped and fell from a cliff.

329
00:20:10,893 --> 00:20:11,893
Really?

330
00:20:12,563 --> 00:20:15,333
That sounds serious. Is she all right now?

331
00:20:17,103 --> 00:20:18,103
Yes.

332
00:20:19,403 --> 00:20:20,403
But...

333
00:20:21,333 --> 00:20:22,733
she mentioned you.

334
00:20:23,773 --> 00:20:24,773
Me?

335
00:20:25,043 --> 00:20:28,273
Hee Ju thinks she got hurt because of you.

336
00:20:30,383 --> 00:20:32,483
Oh, I see.

337
00:20:34,853 --> 00:20:36,153
That's not true, is it?

338
00:20:39,693 --> 00:20:40,693
Right?

339
00:20:40,923 --> 00:20:44,263
You're not the kind of person who would hurt Hee Ju.

340
00:20:44,963 --> 00:20:46,933
If I'd really been serious about it,

341
00:20:47,933 --> 00:20:48,933
she...

342
00:20:49,493 --> 00:20:50,563
would be dead.

343
00:20:53,673 --> 00:20:56,033
But that won't happen anymore.

344
00:20:57,003 --> 00:20:59,873
Everything's going to be all right now, Mi Young.

345
00:21:02,613 --> 00:21:03,613
Let's eat.

346
00:21:24,163 --> 00:21:25,463
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

347
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:30,003
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

348
00:21:30,543 --> 00:21:31,643
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

349
00:21:42,653 --> 00:21:44,753
(15 Missed Calls: Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

350
00:21:54,663 --> 00:21:56,433
Are you really not going to answer?

351
00:21:57,133 --> 00:21:59,063
I only need a moment. Just one minute.

352
00:21:59,403 --> 00:22:01,003
This is so unfair.

353
00:22:01,533 --> 00:22:03,173
What did I do wrong?

354
00:22:05,073 --> 00:22:06,913
Let's not do this, Hee Ju.

355
00:22:12,443 --> 00:22:14,953
- You were home. - Yes, hey...

356
00:22:16,983 --> 00:22:17,983
Have you had dinner?

357
00:22:18,353 --> 00:22:20,123
Yes, I had dinner.

358
00:22:20,853 --> 00:22:21,853
What about you?

359
00:22:22,093 --> 00:22:24,223
Yes, I ate something too.

360
00:22:31,103 --> 00:22:32,603
Shouldn't you get that?

361
00:22:32,833 --> 00:22:34,673
No, it's fine. Don't worry about it.

362
00:22:55,723 --> 00:22:57,263
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

363
00:23:09,473 --> 00:23:10,473
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

364
00:23:13,413 --> 00:23:14,843
(Block Contact)

365
00:23:16,583 --> 00:23:17,583
(Block)

366
00:23:26,893 --> 00:23:28,693
Gosh, seriously.

367
00:23:34,233 --> 00:23:36,333
The person you are calling is unavailable...

368
00:23:37,663 --> 00:23:40,373
You really shouldn't have done that.

369
00:23:47,673 --> 00:23:48,673
Yes.

370
00:23:49,273 --> 00:23:50,743
Can we meet right now?

371
00:24:00,823 --> 00:24:02,053
Are you the one who called?

372
00:24:04,063 --> 00:24:05,193
Don't worry.

373
00:24:05,463 --> 00:24:07,233
I guarantee complete confidentiality.

374
00:24:10,133 --> 00:24:11,133
Let's see it.

375
00:24:17,973 --> 00:24:19,343
No way.

376
00:24:20,073 --> 00:24:21,073
How much do you want?

377
00:24:21,673 --> 00:24:23,883
I don't need any money.

378
00:24:24,143 --> 00:24:26,553
What? Then what do you want?

379
00:24:27,283 --> 00:24:28,283
Hey.

380
00:24:28,683 --> 00:24:32,823
If you just leave, that's a sweet deal for me.

381
00:24:51,803 --> 00:24:53,043
- Hey... - Listen...

382
00:24:56,413 --> 00:24:57,483
You go first.

383
00:24:58,643 --> 00:25:01,053
No. You go first.

384
00:25:03,483 --> 00:25:04,853
You heard, right?

385
00:25:05,023 --> 00:25:07,023
About the upcoming Domestic Affairs Investigation.

386
00:25:08,293 --> 00:25:09,963
Yes, I heard.

387
00:25:13,893 --> 00:25:17,833
Both of us are exhausted from the legal briefs.

388
00:25:18,633 --> 00:25:20,203
For the Domestic Affairs Investigation...

389
00:25:20,273 --> 00:25:21,873
So you're saying we shouldn't be so on edge...

390
00:25:21,933 --> 00:25:23,573
and just take it easy.

391
00:25:24,843 --> 00:25:27,613
Okay, I get it. I'll do that. Don't worry too much.

392
00:25:28,873 --> 00:25:29,913
Thank you.

393
00:25:30,943 --> 00:25:33,883
By the way, was Hee Ju discharged okay?

394
00:25:34,413 --> 00:25:35,413
Yes.

395
00:25:36,213 --> 00:25:37,283
And...

396
00:25:38,483 --> 00:25:40,923
there won't be any more trouble from now on.

397
00:25:41,093 --> 00:25:42,093
Okay.

398
00:25:48,463 --> 00:25:50,733
- Yes, A Ri. - Yes, Kyung Tae.

399
00:25:52,263 --> 00:25:54,303
- What do you mean? - What?

400
00:26:04,313 --> 00:26:05,713
("Falling in Love Isn't a Crime!")

401
00:26:05,783 --> 00:26:07,153
CEO Baek.

402
00:26:07,583 --> 00:26:09,213
What in the world is this?

403
00:26:09,583 --> 00:26:10,583
I don't know.

404
00:26:10,953 --> 00:26:12,823
It looks like someone secretly and maliciously took the photo...

405
00:26:12,823 --> 00:26:14,093
and sent it in.

406
00:26:14,153 --> 00:26:16,723
So what psycho would do this?

407
00:26:18,123 --> 00:26:19,563
But this photo,

408
00:26:19,893 --> 00:26:21,463
it doesn't look like it's photoshopped.

409
00:26:25,003 --> 00:26:26,833
This channel is malicious.

410
00:26:26,903 --> 00:26:29,773
A secret love affair? Does this make any sense?

411
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:32,103
What are we going to do, Mi Young?

412
00:26:32,103 --> 00:26:33,673
What do you mean?

413
00:26:33,743 --> 00:26:35,813
It's just a baseless rumour.

414
00:26:36,273 --> 00:26:39,683
It'll probably die down after a while.

415
00:26:44,183 --> 00:26:45,253
CEO Baek.

416
00:26:47,493 --> 00:26:49,093
We need you to come see this.

417
00:26:49,493 --> 00:26:52,263
We're getting flooded with complaints from customers.

418
00:27:00,673 --> 00:27:03,073
What was just posted isn't true.

419
00:27:04,143 --> 00:27:07,273
- We're just employees... - Yes, a cancellation...

420
00:27:07,843 --> 00:27:08,913
You're cancelling...

421
00:27:10,083 --> 00:27:11,713
It's a rumour...

422
00:27:27,263 --> 00:27:29,833
Ninety percent of the clients with reservations...

423
00:27:29,893 --> 00:27:32,463
have called to cancel.

424
00:27:34,533 --> 00:27:36,473
And the other ten percent...

425
00:27:36,803 --> 00:27:39,343
said they'll think about it and get back to us.

426
00:27:45,013 --> 00:27:48,753
Maybe I should just sue that YouTuber?

427
00:27:49,483 --> 00:27:52,623
Spreading rumours like this without confirming a single fact...

428
00:27:52,723 --> 00:27:54,123
is defamation.

429
00:27:54,393 --> 00:27:57,063
But if you sue that YouTuber,

430
00:27:57,123 --> 00:27:59,063
they'll just dig into your private life...

431
00:27:59,123 --> 00:28:00,193
even more relentlessly.

432
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:03,193
And what if...

433
00:28:03,293 --> 00:28:06,263
they find out you're in the middle of a divorce?

434
00:28:07,173 --> 00:28:08,833
Wouldn't the fallout be even worse?

435
00:28:17,913 --> 00:28:19,443
I'll leave you two alone.

436
00:28:32,023 --> 00:28:34,633
I'm sorry. This must be a big shock.

437
00:28:35,463 --> 00:28:38,333
No, these things happen.

438
00:28:40,833 --> 00:28:41,903
Look...

439
00:28:43,403 --> 00:28:47,143
No matter what anyone says, I don't care.

440
00:28:48,373 --> 00:28:49,643
Because I trust you.

441
00:28:50,613 --> 00:28:54,583
I know you would never betray me when it comes to other men.

442
00:28:55,913 --> 00:28:57,123
I'm certain of that.

443
00:28:58,423 --> 00:28:59,683
Even if you don't trust me.

444
00:29:00,253 --> 00:29:01,253
Really?

445
00:29:02,893 --> 00:29:04,323
Thank you for trusting me.

446
00:29:05,993 --> 00:29:09,063
But seriously, who could have taken this picture?

447
00:29:09,633 --> 00:29:11,463
What kind of psycho would do this?

448
00:29:13,233 --> 00:29:16,303
I don't know if "psycho" is...

449
00:29:16,603 --> 00:29:18,243
the right word...

450
00:29:18,303 --> 00:29:19,703
Of course it is.

451
00:29:26,313 --> 00:29:27,483
Could it be...

452
00:29:29,613 --> 00:29:30,953
Hee Ju?

453
00:29:32,223 --> 00:29:33,553
Did Hee Ju take the photo?

454
00:29:33,853 --> 00:29:34,853
I mean...

455
00:29:35,653 --> 00:29:38,823
I didn't know she would post it online.

456
00:29:38,893 --> 00:29:41,163
So you already knew...

457
00:29:41,233 --> 00:29:43,603
that she took the picture? Since when?

458
00:29:45,333 --> 00:29:46,733
For a while...

459
00:29:48,603 --> 00:29:49,733
Unbelievable.

460
00:29:59,213 --> 00:30:01,513
If I'd really been serious about it,

461
00:30:01,883 --> 00:30:02,883
she...

462
00:30:03,583 --> 00:30:04,683
would be dead.

463
00:30:05,783 --> 00:30:08,293
But that won't happen now.

464
00:30:09,053 --> 00:30:12,223
Everything's going to be all right now, Mi Young.

465
00:30:13,693 --> 00:30:14,833
Hee Ju...

466
00:30:16,263 --> 00:30:18,703
Where is Hee Ju right now?

467
00:30:18,933 --> 00:30:21,773
- What? - I said, where is she?

468
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:24,503
How should I know? I blocked her number.

469
00:30:24,573 --> 00:30:26,303
Call her and check, quickly.

470
00:30:26,373 --> 00:30:29,113
Why? What's with the sudden urgency?

471
00:30:30,113 --> 00:30:32,543
You want to find Hee Ju and throw her in jail, don't you?

472
00:30:32,613 --> 00:30:34,413
Stop talking nonsense and do it.

473
00:30:34,513 --> 00:30:36,183
All right.

474
00:30:36,853 --> 00:30:39,623
I have to unblock her first.

475
00:30:50,633 --> 00:30:53,033
(CEO Calvin Kim)

476
00:31:14,153 --> 00:31:15,393
Take this.

477
00:31:17,193 --> 00:31:18,523
This...

478
00:31:18,663 --> 00:31:20,663
When I gave birth to Mi Young,

479
00:31:20,833 --> 00:31:23,163
Mi Young's father gave this to me as a gift.

480
00:31:24,903 --> 00:31:27,273
Why would you give me something so precious?

481
00:31:27,333 --> 00:31:30,443
That's why I'm giving it to you. Because it's so precious.

482
00:31:34,173 --> 00:31:35,343
Thank you.

483
00:31:35,773 --> 00:31:38,713
For being such a strong source of support for Mi Young.

484
00:31:39,683 --> 00:31:42,283
Please continue to take good care of Mi Young.

485
00:31:43,553 --> 00:31:44,553
Yes.

486
00:31:45,183 --> 00:31:46,323
Don't worry.

487
00:31:47,023 --> 00:31:48,793
I promise I'll protect Mi Young.

488
00:31:53,833 --> 00:31:54,893
Wait.

489
00:31:57,863 --> 00:31:59,163
Take this with you.

490
00:32:01,573 --> 00:32:04,903
My mom gave this to you, so you should keep it.

491
00:32:05,973 --> 00:32:07,143
And...

492
00:32:07,773 --> 00:32:10,413
thank you for remembering the anniversary.

493
00:32:29,963 --> 00:32:30,963
Yes?

494
00:32:31,133 --> 00:32:32,533
Sir, I found him.

495
00:32:45,843 --> 00:32:46,843
Sir?

496
00:33:01,133 --> 00:33:02,133
Hey.

497
00:33:13,373 --> 00:33:15,573
Who are you?

498
00:33:23,553 --> 00:33:24,753
What do you think you're doing?

499
00:33:37,903 --> 00:33:38,903
Secretary Kim.

500
00:33:44,703 --> 00:33:46,203
Wait. Please, spare me.

501
00:33:47,673 --> 00:33:50,813
Why are you doing this to me?

502
00:33:58,353 --> 00:34:02,053
Please, spare me.

503
00:34:03,223 --> 00:34:04,223
Who was it?

504
00:34:07,193 --> 00:34:08,463
Who put you up to this?

505
00:34:14,403 --> 00:34:16,673
How could he not even show up on the day I'm discharged?

506
00:34:16,933 --> 00:34:20,243
He won't be showing up from now on, either.

507
00:34:20,513 --> 00:34:21,513
What did you say?

508
00:34:21,613 --> 00:34:22,643
Won Ho...

509
00:34:23,513 --> 00:34:25,213
isn't going to see you anymore, Hee Ju.

510
00:34:26,043 --> 00:34:29,053
What? He's never going to see me again?

511
00:34:33,923 --> 00:34:35,853
(My Love, Won Ho)

512
00:34:44,863 --> 00:34:46,363
Is Hee Ju still not answering her phone?

513
00:34:46,433 --> 00:34:49,773
It keeps ringing, but I think she's ignoring my calls.

514
00:34:50,103 --> 00:34:52,043
Do you have any idea where she could be?

515
00:34:52,103 --> 00:34:53,503
A close friend's place or...

516
00:34:53,573 --> 00:34:55,943
maybe a favourite spot she hangs out at.

517
00:34:56,013 --> 00:34:58,683
I contacted Man Ju, and she said she doesn't know.

518
00:34:58,743 --> 00:35:00,243
As for her favourite spot...

519
00:35:00,313 --> 00:35:03,583
There's a whiskey bar she frequents, but it's not open yet.

520
00:35:03,853 --> 00:35:04,923
Is that it?

521
00:35:04,983 --> 00:35:07,153
I don't know that much about her either.

522
00:35:08,623 --> 00:35:10,393
But really, why are you acting like this?

523
00:35:10,663 --> 00:35:13,723
It's not like she's in danger again like when she went to that cliff.

524
00:35:14,633 --> 00:35:16,693
She could be in more danger than when she was on that cliff.

525
00:35:17,093 --> 00:35:19,203
- What? - Call her again.

526
00:35:19,203 --> 00:35:20,903
Hurry. Call her again.

527
00:35:21,033 --> 00:35:22,333
Okay, I will.

528
00:35:30,483 --> 00:35:32,743
(Jihwaja Motel)

529
00:35:33,043 --> 00:35:34,213
Oh, for goodness' sake...

530
00:35:34,283 --> 00:35:35,313
Yes, welcome.

531
00:35:35,453 --> 00:35:36,453
What?

532
00:35:36,753 --> 00:35:37,783
Hello.

533
00:35:37,983 --> 00:35:39,583
Wait, what are you doing here?

534
00:35:39,953 --> 00:35:41,353
I'd like a room.

535
00:35:41,753 --> 00:35:42,753
What? A room?

536
00:35:44,263 --> 00:35:45,263
By yourself?

537
00:35:45,893 --> 00:35:47,733
Yes. Is that possible?

538
00:35:48,433 --> 00:35:50,293
Well, I don't really want to,

539
00:35:50,393 --> 00:35:52,203
but I can't be picky about my customers.

540
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:53,903
So yes, it's possible.

541
00:35:55,933 --> 00:35:59,103
Also, can I pay for a month in advance?

542
00:35:59,803 --> 00:36:00,843
A whole month?

543
00:36:02,173 --> 00:36:03,173
Well...

544
00:36:03,843 --> 00:36:04,843
Sure, here...

545
00:36:07,143 --> 00:36:08,153
In a single payment?

546
00:36:08,483 --> 00:36:09,553
Of course.

547
